  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 12-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 antireflection stack on semi-infinite Si substrate at 0 degree incidence with unpolarized illumination. Initialize all 12 layer thicknesses using round-2-best candidate geometry: [308.36, 233.62, 240.00, 350.28, 257.79, 234.77, 244.33, 332.63, 275.66, 250.70, 115.73, 40.52] nm. Apply ±4% Gaussian noise to create initial population. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with hard per-iteration displacement cap of 15 nm per layer. Reduce adaptive learning-rate decay factor to 0.5x nominal to preserve momentum. Optimize for minimum mean reflectance across both wavelength bands (1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm) with equal weighting. Enforce thickness bounds 20-400 nm per layer. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
